# spec-live overlay notes. NO BASE_SHA256 here, deliberately: like
# container/patches/boot-timing and draft-load-filter this NEVER replaces an
# upstream file.
# spec_live.pth is a new file mounted into site-packages; it installs a
# sys.meta_path hook that wraps/extends upstream objects post-import, looked up by
# name. If upstream renames or removes a target the hook no-ops and prints
# "[spec-live] NOT applied ..." -- the server then runs with its static draft depth,
# exactly as upstream does. Nothing to re-derive on snapshot bumps, but re-grep the
# names below on each repin (repin.md section 4).
#
# What it does: lets the MTP draft depth change on a running server
# (GET/POST /spec_tokens) by feeding vLLM's Dynamic SD (vllm#32374) a mutable K.
# The scheduler already picks K per step below num_speculative_tokens, the V2
# worker obeys scheduler_output.num_spec_tokens_to_schedule, and every allocation
# is sized for the maximum -- so the patch only replaces the batch-size lookup
# with one live value and adds the control path.
